The kana decks (data/decks/kana-hiragana.json, kana-katakana.json) are not
derived from EDRDG data. They were authored for this plugin and are released
CC0-1.0: the syllabary itself is not copyrightable.


2. FSRS -- the scheduling algorithm
------------------------------------

bin/kotoba implements the Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler memory model and
uses its published default parameters.

    https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/fsrs4anki
    Algorithm and reference implementations: MIT

The implementation in bin/kotoba was written for this plugin; the model,
formulas and default parameters are the FSRS project's work.


3. The downloadable dictionary
-------------------------------

The optional dictionary pack is downloaded at the user's request from EDRDG:

    JMdict_e.gz        http://ftp.edrdg.org/pub/Nihongo/JMdict_e.gz
    kanjidic2.xml.gz   http://ftp.edrdg.org/pub/Nihongo/kanjidic2.xml.gz
    examples.utf.gz    http://ftp.edrdg.org/pub/Nihongo/examples.utf.gz

JMdict and KANJIDIC2 are CC BY-SA 4.0, as above. examples.utf is the Tanaka
Corpus, distributed by EDRDG under CC BY 2.0.

These are downloaded to the user's own cache and imported into a local
database. They are not redistributed by this plugin, so no ShareAlike
obligation attaches to the plugin tree on their account; the attribution is
given here and on the widget regardless.


4. Fonts
--------

Japanese text is rendered with Noto Sans CJK JP, which ships with the system
(package noto-fonts-cjk, SIL Open Font License 1.1). No font is bundled.
